course: dictionary
lesson: 4362
title: Word study: gunpowder
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun is a naming word for a thing, a place or a person. Gunpowder is a noun. It names a black powder that explodes when it is lit.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. «Long ago tunnels were dug by hand with picks, shovels and gunpowder» tells you that gunpowder was used to break through rock, alongside tools for digging.
explain: Some words also connect to history. Gunpowder appears in the story of the Gunpowder Plot, a failed plan to blow up Parliament, and it is why we have fireworks on Bonfire Night.
fact: Gunpowder is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say some gunpowder rather than a gunpowder.
fact: Gunpowder is a black powder that explodes when lit. It is made from saltpetre, charcoal and sulphur.
fact: «Gunpowder was discovered in China more than a thousand years ago», and it was used for celebrations long before it was used in guns.
fact: The Gunpowder Plot was a failed plan by Guy Fawkes and others to blow up Parliament and King James I.
fact: In science, gunpowder shows a chemical reaction that gives out heat, light and gas very fast.
exercise: What is gunpowder made from? | Water, chalk and wax | Sugar, flour and salt | Iron, copper and tin | *Saltpetre, charcoal and sulphur
exercise: «Gunpowder was discovered in China more than a thousand years ago.» Where was gunpowder first discovered? | *China | Britain | Italy | Egypt
exercise: «It was used for celebrations long before it was used in guns.» What was gunpowder first used for? | *Celebrations, such as fireworks | Digging tunnels | Making paper | Guns and cannons
test: Which event is remembered on Bonfire Night? | Christmas Day | *The Gunpowder Plot | Harvest festival | Midsummer
test: In a science lesson, what does gunpowder show? | *A chemical reaction that gives out heat, light and gas very fast | A plant growing in the dark | A slow cooling of metal | A type of sound wave
exam: Which statement is true? | Gunpowder was invented in Britain for making clocks | Gunpowder has never been used in fireworks | *Gunpowder was discovered in China and used for celebrations before it was used in guns | Gunpowder was first made from sugar and flour
